Axiom

Axiom is a privacy-guard dashboard concept for detecting and redacting sensitive information from recordings and documents. It demonstrates a local-first workflow for reviewing personally identifiable information (PII), credentials, secrets, and personal data before content is shared or stored.



Overview

Axiom presents two connected workflows:

Detection: Start and stop a simulated recording session, scan it, and review categorized sensitive-data findings.

Redaction: Open a simulated document viewer, inspect highlighted findings, redact individual items or all findings, restore them, and simulate exporting a clean copy.

The interface is packaged as a single axiom.html file with embedded styles and JavaScript, so it can be opened directly in a browser without a build step.

Features

Dark, privacy-focused dashboard UI

Simulated recording timer and scanning progress

Detection summary grouped into:

PII, such as Social Security and credit card numbers

Secrets, such as access keys and connection strings

Personal data, such as email addresses and home addresses

Interactive document redaction preview

Individual and bulk redaction controls

Restore-all workflow

In-app alerts and scan status indicators

Keyboard shortcut to start or stop recording: Ctrl+R or Cmd+R

Responsive single-file implementation with no framework or package installation
